{"audio": "galatians-01.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 147467, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 1867, "text": "Galatians, Chapter One."}, {"start_ms": 1867, "end_ms": 20667, "text": "Paul, an apostle, (not of men, neither by man, but by Jesus Christ, and God the Father, who raised him from the dead;) And all the brethren which are with me, unto the churches of Galatia: Grace be to you and peace from God the Father, and from our Lord Jesus Christ, Who gave himself for our sins,"}, {"start_ms": 20667, "end_ms": 28400, "text": "that he might deliver us from this present evil world, according to the will of God and our Father: To whom be glory for ever and ever."}, {"start_ms": 28400, "end_ms": 29067, "text": "Amen."}, {"start_ms": 29067, "end_ms": 41067, "text": "I marvel that ye are so soon removed from him that called you into the grace of Christ unto another gospel: Which is not another; but there be some that trouble you, and would pervert the gospel of Christ."}, {"start_ms": 41067, "end_ms": 49467, "text": "But though we, or an angel from heaven, preach any other gospel unto you than that which we have preached unto you, let him be accursed."}, {"start_ms": 49467, "end_ms": 58000, "text": "As we said before, so say I now again, If any man preach any other gospel unto you than that ye have received, let him be accursed."}, {"start_ms": 58000, "end_ms": 61200, "text": "For do I now persuade men, or God?"}, {"start_ms": 61200, "end_ms": 63200, "text": "or do I seek to please men?"}, {"start_ms": 63200, "end_ms": 67200, "text": "for if I yet pleased men, I should not be the servant of Christ."}, {"start_ms": 67200, "end_ms": 71867, "text": "But I certify you, brethren, that the gospel which was preached of me is not after man."}, {"start_ms": 71867, "end_ms": 78133, "text": "For I neither received it of man, neither was I taught it, but by the revelation of Jesus Christ."}, {"start_ms": 78133, "end_ms": 95333, "text": "For ye have heard of my conversation in time past in the Jews' religion, how that beyond measure I persecuted the church of God, and wasted it: And profited in the Jews' religion above many my equals in mine own nation, being more exceedingly zealous of the traditions of my fathers."}, {"start_ms": 95333, "end_ms": 111733, "text": "But when it pleased God, who separated me from my mother's womb, and called me by his grace, To reveal his Son in me, that I might preach him among the heathen; immediately I conferred not with flesh and blood: Neither went I up to Jerusalem to them which were apostles before me;"}, {"start_ms": 111733, "end_ms": 116267, "text": "but I went into Arabia, and returned again unto Damascus."}, {"start_ms": 116267, "end_ms": 121733, "text": "Then after three years I went up to Jerusalem to see Peter, and abode with him fifteen days."}, {"start_ms": 121733, "end_ms": 126267, "text": "But other of the apostles saw I none, save James the Lord's brother."}, {"start_ms": 126267, "end_ms": 130667, "text": "Now the things which I write unto you, behold, before God, I lie not."}, {"start_ms": 130667, "end_ms": 145467, "text": "Afterwards I came into the regions of Syria and Cilicia; And was unknown by face unto the churches of Judaea which were in Christ: But they had heard only, That he which persecuted us in times past now preacheth the faith which once he destroyed."}, {"start_ms": 145467, "end_ms": 147467, "text": "And they glorified God in me."}], "words": [{"t": "Galatians,", "s": 462, "e": 1044, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 1164, "e": 1506, "si": 0}, {"t": "One.", "s": 1626, "e": 1787, "si": 0}, {"t": "Paul,", "s": 2608, "e": 2908, "si": 1}, {"t": "an", "s": 3068, "e": 3128, "si": 1}, {"t": "apostle,", "s": 3208, "e": 3789, "si": 1}, {"t": "(not", "s": 4410, "e": 4570, "si": 1}, {"t": "of", "s": 4610, "e": 4690, "si": 1}, {"t": "men,", "s": 4770, "e": 5010, "si": 1}, {"t": "neither", "s": 5331, "e": 5631, "si": 1}, {"t": "by", "s": 5711, "e": 5871, "si": 1}, {"t": "man,", 